A||N||12||troydeb||Getting in reverse ?! ||||8||
Z||000000||troydeb||11-15-2001||07:13 PM||||IM looking for some suggestions on why sometimes when i try to shift into reverse (manual) it wont let me either the gears will grind or i can only get in about half way.  All of the other gears shift fine.  Theres only 20,000 on the clutch and its not driven hard.  Any ideas? hopefully something simple  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>Thanks||||reg||8
Z||000001||WampusCat||11-15-2001||07:21 PM||||Never had that on the Fiero, but when my Toyota won't shift into reverse, I put the shifter in the neutral position, let the clutch pedal out, push the clutch back in and shift into reverse.  Don't know why this works but it always does on the truck.||||reg||1
Z||000002||troydeb||11-15-2001||07:25 PM||||i have tried that but no go there. it only seems to do it after its warmed up.  Transaxle fluid?||||reg||1
